{"Title":"An Act relative to the Lafayette Trail","BillNumber":"H3308","DocketNumber":"HD3294","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PJD2","Name":"Peter J. Durant","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJD2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T13:32:15.68"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PJD2","Name":"Peter J. Durant","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJD2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T13:32:15.68"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3308/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Durant of Spencer, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3308) of Peter J. Durant for legislation to designate certain portions of Route 9, Route 20 and Route 32 as the General Lafayette trail.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 2. Chapter 29 of the acts of 1997 is hereby amended by inserting after the first paragraph the following paragraph:-\r\n\tThe following portions of state highway shall be designated and known as the General Lafayette Trail: that portion of Massachusetts Route 9 beginning in the town of Belchertown and continuing easterly\r\n\tuntil the intersection with Massachusetts Route 32 in the town of Ware; that portion of Massachusetts Route 32 beginning in the town of Ware and continuing easterly until the intersection with Massachusetts Route 9 (East Street); that portion of Massachusetts Route 9 beginning in the town of Ware and continuing easterly until the intersection with Stafford Street in the town of Worcester; that portion of Massachusetts Route 20 beginning in the town of Fiskdale at the intersection with Holland Road and continuing easterly until the intersection with Massachusetts Route 131 in the town of Sturbridge; that portion of Massachusetts Route 20 beginning in the town of Sturbridge at the intersection with Hall Road and continuing easterly until the intersection with Stafford Street; that portion of Stafford Street beginning in the town of Sturbridge at the intersection with Massachusetts Route 20 and continuing northeasterly until the intersection with Main Street in the town of Worcester;. The department of highways shall erect and maintain suitable markers bearing said designations.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}